From 4c059dd59b41a22b35d15333de490d1b88c5dbf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:16:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Describe the pixel data and shorten the interface
 text

Say what the pipe of StartFrame carries: the order of the rows, padding,
the samples of each format, depth and byte order, and how a scan in
several passes comes as frames. The text pointed to the started event
for the layout and to nothing for the rest.

Say "network scanner" where it said network printer, split the vendor
and model keys, and drop the account of how the driver is chosen from
the description of ListScanners(), where the portal chooses a driver
based on ranking and functionality is all an application needs.
---
 data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml | 51 ++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
index c6d4a11..21b15f5 100644
--- a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
+++ b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
@@ -116,10 +116,8 @@
         allows it. Applications must not construct ids.
 
         A physical scanner is listed once, however many drivers find it, as
-        a network printer is by both an eSCL and a vendor driver. The portal
-        opens it with the driver that ranks best, and with the next one if
-        that cannot open it, so an application does not see a driver that
-        does not work.
+        a network scanner is by both an eSCL and a vendor driver. The portal
+        chooses a driver based on ranking and functionality.
 
         Keys in the information vardict:
 
@@ -127,9 +125,13 @@
 
           User-visible name.
 
-        * ``vendor`` (``s``), ``model`` (``s``)
+        * ``vendor`` (``s``)
 
-          As reported by the backend.
+          The vendor, as reported by the backend.
+
+        * ``model`` (``s``)
+
+          The model, as reported by the backend.
 
         * ``backend`` (``s``)
 
@@ -372,9 +374,8 @@
         A value of ``{'auto': <true>}`` (an ``a{sv}``) asks the scanner to pick
         the option's value itself, as SANE's ``SANE_ACTION_SET_AUTO``. It is
         only valid for options with the ``automatic`` capability. (D-Bus has
-        no empty structure, so a vardict stands in for a "no value" marker, and
-        leaves room for further per-option modifiers.) An
-        invalid option or value fails the whole call with
+        no empty structure, so a vardict stands in for a "no value" marker.)
+        An invalid option or value fails the whole call with
         ``org.freedesktop.portal.Error.InvalidArgument`` and applies
         nothing after the failing entry. Fails with
         ``org.freedesktop.portal.Error.Busy`` while a frame is in progress.
@@ -420,10 +421,34 @@
         @fd: Read end of a pipe carrying the frame's pixel data
 
         Starts acquiring one frame and returns at once. Subscribe to
-        FrameEvent before calling. The pipe carries raw image data exactly as
-        SANE delivers it (see the ``started`` event for the layout), and is
-        closed by the portal at the end of the frame. End of data on the pipe
-        is not a success signal: wait for the ``finished`` event.
+        FrameEvent before calling. The pipe is closed by the portal at the
+        end of the frame. End of data on the pipe is not a success signal:
+        wait for the ``finished`` event.
+
+        The pipe carries the frame's pixels as SANE delivers them, described
+        by the ``started`` event (see the SANE standard, "Image Data Format"
+        and ``sane_get_parameters``):
+
+        * Rows run from the top of the image down, ``bytes_per_line`` bytes
+          each, and there are ``lines`` of them. A row can end in padding, so
+          ``bytes_per_line`` can be more than the pixels in it need.
+
+        * ``gray``, ``red``, ``green``, ``blue`` and ``ir`` frames have one
+          sample per pixel. ``rgb`` has three, in the order red, green, blue,
+          and ``rgbi`` four, with infrared last. ``grayi`` has two, gray and
+          infrared.
+
+        * ``depth`` is the bits in a sample: 1, 8 or 16. A depth of 1 packs
+          eight pixels to a byte, the first one in the most significant bit.
+          A 16-bit sample is two bytes in the host's byte order, as SANE
+          delivers it. Samples of one pixel are next to each other in a row.
+
+        * A scan in several passes is several frames, one for each of
+          ``red``, ``green`` and ``blue``, and ``last_frame`` is true on the
+          last of them. The application combines them.
+
+        * When ``lines`` is -1 the height is not known in advance, as for a
+          hand scanner, and the frame is as long as the data on the pipe.
 
         Call again after ``finished`` while ``last_frame`` was false (for
         example separate red, green, blue and infrared frames). Fails with
